Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt8183-kukui: give /firmware address cells

Depthcharge adds /firmware/coreboot (and /firmware/chromeos) at boot and
creates /firmware with only an empty "ranges". Since 6.18 the OF core
matches the default bus only when the parent has its own #address-cells
(of_bus_default_match), so of_get_address() returns NULL for the
coreboot node, the platform device has no resource, and coreboot_table
fails with -EINVAL. Without it there is no /sys/firmware/vpd (serial
number, region) and no memconsole.

Declare the node here with the cells depthcharge already uses for the
reg property (2/2, the root values). Depthcharge fills in the existing
node.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8183-kukui.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8183-kukui.dtsi
@@ -21,6 +21,12 @@
 		stdout-path = "serial0:115200n8";
 	};
 
+	firmware {
+		#address-cells = <2>;
+		#size-cells = <2>;
+		ranges;
+	};
+
 	backlight_lcd0: backlight_lcd0 {
 		compatible = "pwm-backlight";
 		pwms = <&pwm0 0 500000>;
